SUMMARY:Rimaqpanpa: Multilingual and Multidisciplinary Seminar on Andean 
 Studies
DESCRIPTION:This two-day\, public Rimaqpanpa (https://as.nyu.edu/research
 -centers/clacs/events/fall-2026/rimaqpanpa-andean-studies-seminar-fall-20
 26.html)—a Quechua term meaning "platform of omens" or "esplanade of di
 alogues"—brings together 11 leading Andean scholars and artists from ar
 ound the world\, who will discuss and disseminate the groundbreaking scho
 larship that has shaped the field of Andean Studies over the last two dec
 ades.  This inaugural Rimaqpanpa also highlights the cultural riches of t
 he Andean world\, featuring the legendary Andean soprano Sylvia Falcón a
 nd the premiere of filmmaker Ramon Rivera-Moret's two short films about A
 ndean sky observers.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This two-day\, public <i><a href="https
 ://as.nyu.edu/research-centers/clacs/events/fall-2026/rimaqpanpa-andean-s
 tudies-seminar-fall-2026.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rimaqpanpa<
 /a></i>—a Quechua term meaning "platform of omens" or "esplanade of dia
 logues"—brings together 11 leading Andean scholars and artists from aro
 und the world\, who will discuss and disseminate the groundbreaking schol
 arship that has shaped the field of Andean Studies over the last two deca
 des.<br /><br />  This inaugural <i>Rimaqpanpa</i> also highlights the cu
 ltural riches of the Andean world\, featuring the legendary Andean sopran
 o Sylvia Falcón and the premiere of filmmaker Ramon Rivera-Moret's two s
 hort films about Andean sky observers.</p>
