BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T203000
LOCATION:Skirball Center for the Performing Arts
GEO:40.729795;-73.997749
SUMMARY:Tom at the Farm
DESCRIPTION:ABOUTTom drives out from the city for his boyfriend's funeral
  and discovers the family never knew their son was gay. His brother inten
 ds to keep it that way. What grows between them is stranger than a stando
 ff: threats that slide into tenderness\, a grieving stranger pulled deepe
 r into a family that will not let him leave or let him be known.Rodrigo P
 ortella stages Michel Marc Bouchard's play on a ring of open earth that c
 omes to stand for a whole country turning back on itself. Winner of the t
 op prizes of the Brazilian stage\, the production has built an acclaimed 
 international trajectory\, with performances in Montreal\, Avignon\, Pari
 s\, Brussels\, a tour across France\, Switzerland and Belgium\, a success
 ful season at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe\, and most recently in South 
 Korea. It now makes its U.S. premiere at NYU Skirball on its way to Londo
 n's Barbican.ADVISORY    This production features sexual content and nudi
 ty.  RUN TIME    Approximately 2 hours\, no intermission  LANGUAGE    Thi
 s production is performed in Portuguese with English subtitles.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p id="intro-heading" class="text-header-2 u
 ppercase leading-none" style="text-align: left\;"><strong>ABOUT</strong><
 /p><p class="text-header-2 uppercase leading-none"><span style="font-size
 : 16px\; font-weight: 400\;">Tom drives out from the city for his boyfrie
 nd's funeral and discovers the family never knew their son was gay. His b
 rother intends to keep it that way. What grows between them is stranger t
 han a standoff: threats that slide into tenderness\, a grieving stranger 
 pulled deeper into a family that will not let him leave or let him be kno
 wn.</span></p><p class="text-header-2 uppercase leading-none"><strong>Rod
 rigo Portella</strong> stages <strong>Michel Marc Bouchard</strong>'s pla
 y on a ring of open earth that comes to stand for a whole country turning
  back on itself. Winner of the top prizes of the Brazilian stage\, the pr
 oduction has built an acclaimed international trajectory\, with performan
 ces in Montreal\, Avignon\, Paris\, Brussels\, a tour across France\, Swi
 tzerland and Belgium\, a successful season at the Edinburgh Festival Frin
 ge\, and most recently in South Korea. It now makes its U.S. premiere at 
 NYU Skirball on its way to London's Barbican.</p><div class="wp-block-gro
 up is-layout-grid wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0fed8f92 wp-block-gro
 up-is-layout-grid"><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>ADVISORY</strong
 ><br />    This production features sexual content and nudity.  </p><p cl
 ass="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>RUN TIME</strong><br />    Approximately
  2 hours\, no intermission  </p><p class="wp-container-content-fed0428f w
 p-block-paragraph"><strong>LANGUAGE</strong><br />    This production is 
 performed in Portuguese with English subtitles.  </p></div>
