DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T133000
LOCATION:Global Center for Academic and Spiritual Life\; Suite 491
GEO:40.7299;-73.9982
SUMMARY:Faculty and Staff Luncheon with Casper ter Kuile
DESCRIPTION:In the shifting landscape of education and technology\, what 
 we owe each other isn't always clear.  Join us for a faculty and staff lu
 ncheon with Casper ter Kuile\, author of The Power of Ritual (https://www
 .harpercollins.com/products/the-power-of-ritual-casper-ter-kuile?variant=
 32894732140578) and GSL Scholar-in-Residence\, to explore practical ways 
 to honor our duty of care as educators and leaders\, especially in the ag
 e of AI. Inspired by his forthcoming research on covenant relationships a
 s spiritual technology\, Casper draws on the wisdom of ancient traditions
  to help us determine what we owe each other in the modern world.  Lunch 
 will be provided. Please note that this gathering is intended for NYU fac
 ulty and staff.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In the shifting landscape of education 
 and technology\, what we owe each other isn't always clear.</p><p>  Join 
 us for a faculty and staff luncheon with Casper ter Kuile\, author of <em
 ><a href="https://www.harpercollins.com/products/the-power-of-ritual-casp
 er-ter-kuile?variant=32894732140578" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The P
 ower of Ritual</a></em> and GSL Scholar-in-Residence\, to explore practic
 al ways to honor our duty of care as educators and leaders\, especially i
 n the age of AI. Inspired by his forthcoming research on covenant relatio
 nships as spiritual technology\, Casper draws on the wisdom of ancient tr
 aditions to help us determine what we owe each other in the modern world.
 </p><p>  Lunch will be provided. Please note that this gathering is inten
 ded for NYU faculty and staff.&#160\;</p>
