DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T121500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T131500
LOCATION:NYU SPS Midtown Center\, 20 West 43rd Street\, 10th Floor
SUMMARY:The Culture of Purpose - Book Talk
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation about purpose\, trust\, and leader
 ship in the age of AI.RSVP HERE (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQ
 LSdO_Jt15SCVAeJjQmI2B5URZYIM3FfQpeilpkBiIV-tZSe4zw/viewform)  The NYU SPS
  Division of Programs in Business (DPB) invites the NYU community to a co
 nversation with Pascal Wiscour-Conter\, author of The Culture of Purpose:
  How to Communicate in the Age of Intelligence.  As part of DPB's Industr
 y Connection Series\, Wiscour-Conter will explore how leaders can use sto
 rytelling to shape culture\, build trust\, and help people navigate uncer
 tainty. In an AI-driven world overflowing with content\, being heard take
 s more than speaking louder. Drawing on three years of interdisciplinary 
 research\, his book offers a practical framework for communicating with p
 urpose\, connecting with audiences\, and using AI to strengthen human cre
 ativity and judgment.Pascal Wiscour-Conter is an international entreprene
 ur\, advisor\, and author whose career spans finance\, maritime entrepren
 eurship\, and the entertainment industry. He specializes in corporate sto
 rytelling through Pascalogy and serves as Community Officer and a Strateg
 ic Communication faculty member at the Luxembourg School of Business.Date
 : Tuesday\, October 13\, 2026Time: 12:15–1:15 p.m. EDTLocation: NYU SPS
  Midtown Center\, 20 West 43rd Street\, 10th Floor\, Room 1026 (https://w
 ww.google.com/maps/search/20+West+43rd+Street\,+10th+Floor\,+Room+1026?en
 try=gmail&amp\;source=g)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for a conversation about purpos
 e\, trust\, and leadership in the age of AI.</p><p><strong><a href="https
 ://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdO_Jt15SCVAeJjQmI2B5URZYIM3FfQpeilpk
 BiIV-tZSe4zw/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RSVP HERE</a></stro
 ng></p><p>  The NYU SPS Division of Programs in Business (DPB) invites th
 e NYU community to a conversation with <strong>Pascal Wiscour-Conter</str
 ong>\, author of <i>The Culture of Purpose: How to Communicate in the Age
  of Intelligence.</i><br /><br />  As part of DPB's <strong>Industry Conn
 ection Series</strong>\, Wiscour-Conter will explore how leaders can use 
 storytelling to shape culture\, build trust\, and help people navigate un
 certainty. In an AI-driven world overflowing with content\, being heard t
 akes more than speaking louder. Drawing on three years of interdisciplina
 ry research\, his book offers a practical framework for communicating wit
 h purpose\, connecting with audiences\, and using AI to strengthen human 
 creativity and judgment.<br /><br /><strong>Pascal Wiscour-Conter</strong
 > is an international entrepreneur\, advisor\, and author whose career sp
 ans finance\, maritime entrepreneurship\, and the entertainment industry.
  He specializes in corporate storytelling through Pascalogy and serves as
  Community Officer and a Strategic Communication faculty member at the Lu
 xembourg School of Business.<br /><br /><strong>Date</strong>: Tuesday\, 
 October 13\, 2026<br /><strong>Time</strong>: 12:15–1:15 p.m. EDT<br />
 <strong>Location</strong>: NYU SPS Midtown Center\, <a href="https://www.
 google.com/maps/search/20+West+43rd+Street\,+10th+Floor\,+Room+1026?entry
 =gmail&amp\;source=g" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=
 https://www.google.com/maps/search/20%2BWest%2B43rd%2BStreet\,%2B10th%2BF
 loor\,%2BRoom%2B1026?entry%3Dgmail%26source%3Dg&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;us
 t=1789828312549000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3ugBRBJpG-OGgHSmoVELZC">20 West 43rd St
 reet\, 10th Floor\, Room 1026</a></p>
