LOCATION:Remote
SUMMARY:Managing your research and bibliographies - EndNote
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to organize your research by using an easy personal
  database called EndNote. The workshop will get you set up with your very
  own database\, show you the basics of adding to and maintaining your dat
 abase\, and show you how to automatically create bibliographies in your d
 esired style (APA\, MLA\, etc) directly from your account.Not sure which 
 tool to try? Check out this comparison. Or attend a "How Do I Choose?" se
 ssion.This class will be held on Zoom and the link will be sent before th
 e workshop. This workshop will NOT be recorded.To ensure that your class 
 experience is as beneficial as possible\, please download EndNote to your
  computer prior to the class. Instructions for downloading EndNote: https
 ://guides.nyu.edu/endnote (https://guides.nyu.edu/endnote)NYU Libraries i
 s committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with di
 sabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email lib-refer
 ence@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses a
 nd facilities.
