DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T153000
LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 7th Floor\, Rm. 745\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Mindfulness Moment at Bobst
DESCRIPTION:"Natural awareness invites us to rest in a sense of being tha
 t's always present within us and accessible in each moment" - Diana Winst
 onTake a mindfulness moment and join us in community for a series of 30-m
 inute meditation sessions where we will explore the practice of meditatio
 n. Our practice this semester will be centered on using objects: plants\,
  tea\, rocks\, as a point of focus and contemplation. The sessions will o
 ffer you techniques that will help you to center yourself to stay focused
  and grounded as you navigate through the semester.These sessions are par
 t of an ongoing series of community meditations that will happen througho
 ut the semester. Please check the Library Events calendar for our upcomin
 g sessions. Registration appreciated\, walk-ins welcome.NYU Libraries is 
 committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disa
 bilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email lib-referen
 ce@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and
  facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:"Natural awareness invites us to rest in a s
 ense of being that's always present within us and accessible in each mome
 nt" - Diana Winston<br />Take a mindfulness moment and join us in communi
 ty for a series of 30-minute meditation sessions where we will explore th
 e practice of meditation. Our practice this semester will be centered on 
 using objects: plants\, tea\, rocks\, as a point of focus and contemplati
 on. The sessions will offer you techniques that will help you to center y
 ourself to stay focused and grounded as you navigate through the semester
 .<br />These sessions are part of an ongoing series of community meditati
 ons that will happen throughout the semester. Please check the Library Ev
 ents calendar for our upcoming sessions. Registration appreciated\, walk-
 ins welcome.<br />NYU Libraries is committed to providing reasonable acco
 mmodations to individuals with disabilities. If you have an accommodation
  request\, please email lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are a
 lways welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
