SUMMARY:Fall Welcome Social
DESCRIPTION:New and returning Society of Retired Faculty members\, join u
 s for our annual Fall Welcome Social! Join us on Tuesday\, October 13th f
 rom 4-5:30 pm\, at 245 Mercer Street to mingle with new and returning ret
 ired faculty members and enjoy refreshments under our big tent in front o
 f the Work Life office.The Society aims to promote continued connection w
 ith the University after retirement\, foster a sense of community\, and p
 rovide a space for retirees to pursue intellectual interests and engage i
 n volunteer opportunities. We envision the Society of Retired Faculty as 
 a professional and social fellowship for those interested in maintaining 
 a relationship with fellow retirees and the University at large.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  New and returning Society of Retired Fa
 culty members\, join us for our annual Fall Welcome Social! Join us on Tu
 esday\, October 13th from 4-5:30 pm\, at 245 Mercer Street to mingle with
  new and returning retired faculty members and enjoy refreshments under o
 ur big tent in front of the Work Life office.</p><p><em>The Society aims 
 to promote continued connection with the University after retirement\, fo
 ster a sense of community\, and provide a space for retirees to pursue in
 tellectual interests and engage in volunteer opportunities. We envision t
 he Society of Retired Faculty as a professional and social fellowship for
  those interested in maintaining a relationship with fellow retirees and 
 the University at large.</em></p>
