SUMMARY:UNDIVIDED Screening: Latter-Day Saint Stories
DESCRIPTION:How do we create a more perfect union at a time when our coun
 try is so deeply divided? Join us for a screening of episode three from a
  new docuseries\, UNDIVIDED. This episode will feature stories from Latte
 r-day Saint communities\, also known as Mormons. The screening will be fo
 llowed by a panel discussion with leading scholars and creatives. UNDIVID
 ED invites us to reshape the narrative we tell ourselves about our countr
 y and about one another. Our discussion panel will address how to navigat
 e American identity at the intersection of religion and politics in today
 's climate.  Panelists include Simran Jeet Singh\, Assistant Professor of
  Interreligious Histories at Union Theological Seminary and the host of U
 NDIVIDED\; Jack Gordon\, the director of Undivided\; and Janae Smith\, an
  interfaith scholar and graduate student at NYU. The panel discussion wil
 l be moderated by Brett Krutzsch\, the associate director of the Center f
 or Religion and Media at NYU.  Presented by the Center for Religion and M
 edia and the Center for Global Spiritual Life at NYU. Free and open to th
 e public. &#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  How do we create a more perfect union a
 t a time when our country is so deeply divided? Join us for a screening o
 f episode three from a new docuseries\, <em>UNDIVIDED</em>. This episode 
 will feature stories from Latter-day Saint communities\, also known as Mo
 rmons. The screening will be followed by a panel discussion with leading 
 scholars and creatives. <em>UNDIVIDED</em> invites us to reshape the narr
 ative we tell ourselves about our country and about one another. Our disc
 ussion panel will address how to navigate American identity at the inters
 ection of religion and politics in today's climate.</p><p>  Panelists inc
 lude Simran Jeet Singh\, Assistant Professor of Interreligious Histories 
 at Union Theological Seminary and the host of <em>UNDIVIDED</em>\; Jack G
 ordon\, the director of Undivided\; and Janae Smith\, an interfaith schol
 ar and graduate student at NYU. The panel discussion will be moderated by
  Brett Krutzsch\, the associate director of the Center for Religion and M
 edia at NYU.</p><p>  Presented by the Center for Religion and Media and t
 he Center for Global Spiritual Life at NYU. Free and open to the public. 
 &#160\;</p>
