SUMMARY:Supplemental Learning Group - Organic Chemistry II (Tosovska)
DESCRIPTION:Supplemental Learning Groups (SLGs) are lecture specific and 
 give you a chance to practice and test your understanding of the material
  from the past week's lecture(s) in a collaborative group environment. Th
 is is process-based learning\, meaning if you continue to attend\, your l
 earning will compound over the course of the semester. One time attendanc
 e will likely not be very helpful.&#160\;In order for this to be effectiv
 e:- You must come ready to collaborate.- You must come ready to speak.- Y
 ou must be active.&#160\;This will be a framework that you might not be u
 sed to. In this space\, the primary aim is to construct knowledge\, which
  can feel frustrating.Hosted by: University Learning CenterAdditional Inf
 ormation can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12724084 (https://
 engage.nyu.edu/event/12724084)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Supplemental Learning Groups (SLGs) are lect
 ure specific and give you a chance to practice and test your understandin
 g of the material from the past week's lecture(s) in a collaborative grou
 p environment. This is process-based learning\, meaning if you continue t
 o attend\, your learning will compound over the course of the semester. O
 ne time attendance will likely not be very helpful.<br />&#160\;<br />In 
 order for this to be effective:<br />- You must come ready to collaborate
 .<br />- You must come ready to speak.- You must be active.<br />&#160\;<
 br />This will be a framework that you might not be used to. In this spac
 e\, the primary aim is to construct knowledge\, which can feel frustratin
 g.<br />Hosted by: University Learning Center<br />Additional Information
  can be found at: <a href="https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12724084" target=
