LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 7th Floor\, Rm. 745\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Choosing Reliable Sources : How Do You Know? Let's Get Critical: 
 Arts & Humanities Research Day
DESCRIPTION:In our current information landscape\, it can be hard to know
  if something is "real" or "fake." An alternative strategy is to reframe 
 the question as "Is this a reliable source?" This strategy for determinin
 g which sources to use in your research can make your life easier and you
 r scholarship stronger. In this workshop\, we will discuss several factor
 s that should be considered when evaluating the reliability or credibilit
 y of a source. We will practice critically examining citations and using 
 our own sense of judgment to make decisions.Stay after the workshop for f
 ree coffee\, treats\, and conversation!NYU Libraries is committed to prov
 iding reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you 
 have an accommodation request\, please email lib-reference@nyu.edu. Addit
 ionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:In our current information landscape\, it ca
 n be hard to know if something is "real" or "fake." An alternative strate
 gy is to reframe the question as "Is this a reliable source?" This strate
 gy for determining which sources to use in your research can make your li
 fe easier and your scholarship stronger. In this workshop\, we will discu
 ss several factors that should be considered when evaluating the reliabil
 ity or credibility of a source. We will practice critically examining cit
 ations and using our own sense of judgment to make decisions.<br />Stay a
 fter the workshop for free coffee\, treats\, and conversation!<br />NYU L
 ibraries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individua
 ls with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email
  lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's 
 campuses and facilities.
