SUMMARY:So You Wanna Start a Substack? Substack As Public Scholarship
DESCRIPTION:A quick introduction to creative research communicationCuriou
 s about Substack but unsure where to begin? More than a newsletter platfo
 rm\, Substack has become a space for scholars\, writers\, and creators to
  share research\, build communities\, and experiment with public scholars
 hip outside traditional publishing.In this introductory session\, we'll e
 xplore what Substack is\, how academics and public scholars are using it\
 , and how it can complement your research\, teaching\, and creative pract
 ice. We'll also discuss practical considerations\, from publication workf
 lows to audience building.You'll leave with:An understanding of how Subst
 ack fits into the public scholarship landscapeExamples of effective schol
 arly and creative Substack publicationsPractical tips for getting started
  with your own publicationThis event is part of a series of bite-size con
 tent from the Open Knowledge department.NYU Libraries is committed to pro
 viding reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you
  have an accommodation request\, please email open.knowledge@nyu.edu. Add
 itionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:A quick introduction to creative research co
 mmunication<br />Curious about Substack but unsure where to begin? More t
 han a newsletter platform\, Substack has become a space for scholars\, wr
 iters\, and creators to share research\, build communities\, and experime
 nt with public scholarship outside traditional publishing.<br />In this i
 ntroductory session\, we'll explore what Substack is\, how academics and 
 public scholars are using it\, and how it can complement your research\, 
 teaching\, and creative practice. We'll also discuss practical considerat
 ions\, from publication workflows to audience building.<br />You'll leave
  with:<br />An understanding of how Substack fits into the public scholar
 ship landscape<br />Examples of effective scholarly and creative Substack
  publications<br />Practical tips for getting started with your own publi
 cation<br />This event is part of a series of bite-size content from the 
 Open Knowledge department.<br />NYU Libraries is committed to providing r
 easonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you have an
  accommodation request\, please email open.knowledge@nyu.edu. Additionall
 y\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
