LOCATION:NYU Florence - Villa Sassetti
SUMMARY:Screening of "Billi il cowboy"
DESCRIPTION:It is the late 1960s\, and in the Roman countryside\, next to
  the construction sites of the burgeoning working-class suburbs\, dozens 
 of western films were being shot. Billi is twelve years old\; she rides h
 orses and dreams of being a cowboy. When a casting agent shows up looking
  for young extras to do some stunt work\, Billi knows this is her big cha
 nce. Her family\, however\, thinks otherwise.  (Drama\, 15'\, Italy\, 202
 4)DIRECTOR'S NOTE  Cowboy Billi is about a precise moment in life: the en
 d of childhood. Most children leave certain things behind and gain others
 \, but for Billi\, a kid whose true gender identity has lived safely insi
 de the game of 'playing cowboy\,' growing up threatens to take away a lar
 ge part of who this kid is. Moving beyond the binary of conforming or reb
 elling\, the film sets out to show the power of a free spirit and of self
 -determination.  Fede Gianni (b. 1986) is a trans screenwriter and direct
 or whose work has garnered international acclaim. His short films have be
 en screened at prestigious international festivals and have earned awards
  from the Directors Guild of America\, Vimeo\, and The Gotham (formerly k
 nown as IFP). His latest short film\, "Cowboy Billi\," premiered at the 3
 9th Critic's Week at the Venice International Film Festival. The feature-
 length expansion of "Cowboy Billi" has been selected for the 2025 Ikusmir
 a Berriak residency at the San Sebastian Film Festival. In addition to hi
 s filmmaking\, Gianni teaches film at John Cabot University in Rome and N
 ew York University in Florence.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  It is the late 1960s\, and in the Roman
  countryside\, next to the construction sites of the burgeoning working-c
 lass suburbs\, dozens of western films were being shot. Billi is twelve y
 ears old\; she rides horses and dreams of being a cowboy. When a casting 
 agent shows up looking for young extras to do some stunt work\, Billi kno
 ws this is her big chance. Her family\, however\, thinks otherwise.<br />
   (Drama\, 15'\, Italy\, 2024)</p><p><strong>DIRECTOR'S NOTE</strong></p>
 <p>  Cowboy Billi is about a precise moment in life: the end of childhood
 . Most children leave certain things behind and gain others\, but for Bil
 li\, a kid whose true gender identity has lived safely inside the game of
  'playing cowboy\,' growing up threatens to take away a large part of who
  this kid is. Moving beyond the binary of conforming or rebelling\, the f
 ilm sets out to show the power of a free spirit and of self-determination
 .</p><p>  Fede Gianni (b. 1986) is a trans screenwriter and director whos
 e work has garnered international acclaim. His short films have been scre
 ened at prestigious international festivals and have earned awards from t
 he Directors Guild of America\, Vimeo\, and The Gotham (formerly known as
  IFP). His latest short film\, "Cowboy Billi\," premiered at the 39th Cri
 tic's Week at the Venice International Film Festival. The feature-length 
 expansion of "Cowboy Billi" has been selected for the 2025 Ikusmira Berri
 ak residency at the San Sebastian Film Festival. In addition to his filmm
 aking\, Gianni teaches film at John Cabot University in Rome and New York
  University in Florence.</p>
