LOCATION:Remote
SUMMARY:Managing your research and bibliographies - ZOTERO
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to organize your research by using an open-source c
 itation management tool called Zotero. The workshop will get you set up\,
  show you the basics of adding to and maintaining your database\, and sho
 w you how to automatically create bibliographies in your desired style (A
 PA\, MLA\, etc) as you write.In this session\, you will learn how to:Down
 load and navigate the Zotero appImport citation information with a variet
 y of strategiesConfidently craft citations and bibliographiesUnderstand w
 hy we citeConsider setting up efficient integrations and automationsNot s
 ure which tool to try? Check out this comparison. Or attend a "How Do I C
 hoose?" session.This class will be held on Zoom and the link will be sent
  the 3 hours before the workshop. This workshop will NOT be recorded.NYU 
 Libraries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individu
 als with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please emai
 l lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's
  campuses and facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Learn how to organize your research by using
  an open-source citation management tool called Zotero. The workshop will
  get you set up\, show you the basics of adding to and maintaining your d
 atabase\, and show you how to automatically create bibliographies in your
  desired style (APA\, MLA\, etc) as you write.<br />In this session\, you
  will learn how to:<br />Download and navigate the Zotero app<br />Import
  citation information with a variety of strategies<br />Confidently craft
  citations and bibliographies<br />Understand why we cite<br />Consider s
 etting up efficient integrations and automations<br />Not sure which tool
  to try? Check out this comparison. Or attend a "How Do I Choose?" sessio
 n.<br />This class will be held on Zoom and the link will be sent the 3 h
 ours before the workshop. This workshop will NOT be recorded.<br />NYU Li
 braries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individual
 s with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email 
 lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's c
 ampuses and facilities.
