DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T150000
LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 7th Floor\, Rm. 745\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Tracking Down Citations: Let's Get Critical: Arts & Humanities Re
 search Day: How Do You Know?
DESCRIPTION:You're doing some research and you just spotted a citation fo
 r a promising-looking source. But how do you know if that source is legit
 imate? In this workshop\, we'll talk about the importance of training a c
 ritical eye on the citations you encounter in your research process. We'l
 l practice tracking down citations\, identifying the key components of re
 ferences\, and evaluating them for the presence of AI hallucinations. We'
 ll also discuss the importance of assessing the content once you track it
  down.Free lunch will be served from 12:30-2:00 in room 745\, so come a b
 it earlier if you'd like some pizza!NYU Libraries is committed to providi
 ng reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you hav
 e an accommodation request\, please email lib-reference@nyu.edu. Addition
 ally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:You're doing some research and you just spot
 ted a citation for a promising-looking source. But how do you know if tha
 t source is legitimate? In this workshop\, we'll talk about the importanc
 e of training a critical eye on the citations you encounter in your resea
 rch process. We'll practice tracking down citations\, identifying the key
  components of references\, and evaluating them for the presence of AI ha
 llucinations. We'll also discuss the importance of assessing the content 
 once you track it down.<br />Free lunch will be served from 12:30-2:00 in
  room 745\, so come a bit earlier if you'd like some pizza!<br />NYU Libr
 aries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individuals 
 with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email li
 b-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's cam
 puses and facilities.
