LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 6th Floor\, Rm. 617\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Intermediate Git and GitHub
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever encountered a "merge conflict" in your Git repo
 sitory\, and it frustrated you so much you had to copy your code\, delete
  the whole folder\, and re-download it? NO MORE! Come learn how to rectif
 y merge conflicts in Git repositories\, when and how to create branches f
 or collaboration\, and how to create pull requests so your code can be me
 rged into a main code base with Data Services. This workshop will help yo
 u expand on your Git skills to help better manage these workflows\, espec
 ially between collaborators.Prerequisites: proficient with Git clone\, ad
 d\, commit\, push\, pullTech requirements: a GitHub account\, Git install
 ed on the laptop you will use in the workshop\, and an SSH key on that la
 ptop that authenticates to your GitHub account
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Have you ever encountered a "merge conflict"
  in your Git repository\, and it frustrated you so much you had to copy y
 our code\, delete the whole folder\, and re-download it? NO MORE! Come le
 arn how to rectify merge conflicts in Git repositories\, when and how to 
 create branches for collaboration\, and how to create pull requests so yo
 ur code can be merged into a main code base with Data Services. This work
 shop will help you expand on your Git skills to help better manage these 
 workflows\, especially between collaborators.<br />Prerequisites: profici
 ent with Git clone\, add\, commit\, push\, pull<br />Tech requirements: a
  GitHub account\, Git installed on the laptop you will use in the worksho
 p\, and an SSH key on that laptop that authenticates to your GitHub accou
 nt
