SUMMARY:CTF 101: From Player to Challenge Creator
DESCRIPTION:Stop just solving challenges and learn how to build them. CTF
  101 is a hands-on workshop tailored for players\, club organizers\, and 
 aspiring security educators ready to transition from competitors to chall
 enge authors.Whether you are preparing internal challenges for NYU Cybers
 ecurity Club meetings\, regional qualifiers\, or major competitive events
 \, this session covers the complete lifecycle of secure challenge develop
 ment.What You Will CoverDesign &amp\; Balance: Craft realistic scenarios\
 , control difficulty curves\, and prevent unintended solutions or guessin
 g games.Core Tracks &amp\; Infrastructure: Explore live web and crypto de
 mos\, deploy challenges using Docker containers\, and manage remote servi
 ce runners.QA &amp\; Documentation: Implement rigorous debugging workflow
 s\, peer reviews\, and write up official solutions.PrerequisitesA laptop 
 with administrative access and a Linux/Unix environment (native or virtua
 lized).Docker and Docker Compose installed.Basic familiarity with command
 -line tools\, scripting (Python or Bash)\, and fundamental security conce
 pts.Hosted by: Cybersecurity ClubOnline Location: https://osiris.link/csc
 -events (https://osiris.link/csc-events)Additional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12846421 (https://engage.nyu.edu/even
 t/12846421)
