 allenges for NYU Cybersecurity Club meetings\, regional qualifiers\, or m
 ajor competitive events\, this session covers the complete lifecycle of s
 ecure challenge development.<br />What You Will Cover<br />Design &amp\; 
 Balance: Craft realistic scenarios\, control difficulty curves\, and prev
 ent unintended solutions or guessing games.<br />Core Tracks &amp\; Infra
 structure: Explore live web and crypto demos\, deploy challenges using Do
 cker containers\, and manage remote service runners.<br />QA &amp\; Docum
 entation: Implement rigorous debugging workflows\, peer reviews\, and wri
 te up official solutions.<br />Prerequisites<br />A laptop with administr
 ative access and a Linux/Unix environment (native or virtualized).<br />D
 ocker and Docker Compose installed.<br />Basic familiarity with command-l
 ine tools\, scripting (Python or Bash)\, and fundamental security concept
