DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T180000
LOCATION:Elmer Holmes Bobst Library\, Room 745
SUMMARY:Meditations on Earth
DESCRIPTION:These meditations will be led by Bart van Melik (https://www.
 bartvanmelik.com/)\, Jane O'Mahony\, and Qahtan Al Jammali weaving mindfu
 lness with reflections on our environment. Delve into the nature of chang
 e\, from the expansion of the universe\, the climate\, to the nature of t
 hought itself.  The session starts with a theme talk\, followed by mindfu
 lness movement rooted in Qi Gong\, seated meditation\, and reflections.  
 Whether this is your very first meditation or are a longtime practitioner
 \, all are welcome.  Cushions\, benches\, chairs\, and backjacks are avai
 lable. Registration is not required.  Sessions are part of an ongoing com
 munity meditation series hosted by the Office of Sustainability and NYU L
 ibraries on Wednesdays throughout the academic year.  Meditations on Eart
 h is in alignment with the NYU IRL Initiative. This event will be device-
 free. We invite you to silence your devices\, turn off notifications\, an
 d embrace the opportunity to be fully present and engaged.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  These meditations will be led by <a hre
 f="https://www.bartvanmelik.com/">Bart van Melik</a>\, Jane O'Mahony\, an
 d Qahtan Al Jammali weaving mindfulness with reflections on our environme
 nt. Delve into the nature of change\, from the expansion of the universe\
 , the climate\, to the nature of thought itself.</p><p>  The session star
 ts with a theme talk\, followed by mindfulness movement rooted in Qi Gong
 \, seated meditation\, and reflections.</p><p>  Whether this is your very
  first meditation or are a longtime practitioner\, all are welcome.</p><p
 >  Cushions\, benches\, chairs\, and backjacks are available. Registratio
 n is not required.</p><p>  Sessions are part of an ongoing community medi
 tation series hosted by the Office of Sustainability and NYU Libraries on
  Wednesdays throughout the academic year.</p><p>  Meditations on Earth is
  in alignment with the NYU IRL Initiative. This event will be device-free
 . We invite you to silence your devices\, turn off notifications\, and em
 brace the opportunity to be fully present and engaged.</p>
