DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T183000
LOCATION:726 Broadway\, 6th Floor\, New York\, NY 10003
GEO:40.729421;-73.993165
SUMMARY:An American Miseducation: A Talk with Journalist/Writer Mara Marq
 ues Cavallaro
DESCRIPTION:Join writer\, reporter\, and translator Mara Marques Cavallar
 o (https://www.maracavallaro.com/) for An American Miseducation\, a talk 
 exploring playful and innovative approaches to writing about gravely seri
 ous subjects. Centered on an essay\, the session will examine the work's 
 form and content and invite participants to put these ideas into practice
  through an exercise.  Based in New York City\, Cavallaro has reported on
  inhumane conditions in ICE detention\, police violence\, immigration\, e
 nvironmental racism\, underground abortion networks\, and the legacies of
  Latin American dictatorships. Her work has appeared in The Nation\, El T
 ecolote\, and Jacobin. She is the Director of the Incarcerated Writers In
 itiative at Columbia University School of the Arts and the editor of its 
 annual anthology\, Exchange.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join writer\, reporter\, and translator
  <a href="https://www.maracavallaro.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
 Mara Marques Cavallaro</a> for <em>An American Miseducation</em>\, a talk
  exploring playful and innovative approaches to writing about gravely ser
 ious subjects. Centered on an essay\, the session will examine the work's
  form and content and invite participants to put these ideas into practic
 e through an exercise.</p><p>  Based in New York City\, Cavallaro has rep
 orted on inhumane conditions in ICE detention\, police violence\, immigra
 tion\, environmental racism\, underground abortion networks\, and the leg
 acies of Latin American dictatorships. Her work has appeared in <em>The N
 ation</em>\, <em>El Tecolote</em>\, and <em>Jacobin</em>. She is the Dire
 ctor of the Incarcerated Writers Initiative at Columbia University School
  of the Arts and the editor of its annual anthology\, <em>Exchange</em>.<
 /p>
