SUMMARY:Careers in Sustainability
DESCRIPTION:Join the NYU SPS Center for Global Affairs (http://www.scps.n
 yu.edu/academics/departments/global-affairs.html) and the Center on Globa
 l Energy Policy at Columbia University SIPA's Women in Energy (https://ur
 ldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__womeninenergy.energypolicy.col
 umbia.edu_&amp\;d=DwMFaQ&amp\;c=slrrB7dE8n7gBJbeO0g-IQ&amp\;r=2E2QVW4SeE5
 863MOhaARuDwTA4zaZ-gmdzWI3bY66Co&amp\;m=hkGo3aJolAPR36XlSCKKZtJlT4dLk8gC2
 sFymsFxa3qlfLn1Wc5v5cmcNatp7gLN&amp\;s=lngGPTXnK7-8MhGwrQ1jeXWs_32wC8QI9s
 nbbWpGKYQ&amp\;e=) initiative (WIE) for a dynamic conversation on the exp
 anding career opportunities within the sustainability ecosystem.  The con
 versations around climate action\, sustainability\, and the future of wor
 k are more relevant than ever. As global efforts to decarbonize accelerat
 e—and as industries like real estate and finance adapt to changing poli
 cy landscapes\, emerging regulations\, and new technologies—sustainabil
 ity has become a core driver across nearly every sector.  Whether you're 
 exploring entry-level opportunities or seeking to pivot your focus toward
  a low-carbon future\, this discussion will offer valuable insights and p
 ractical guidance on how to make a lasting impact in this critical\, rapi
 dly evolving field.Moderator:Aida Rodriquez\, Board Member and Former CEO
  and CSO\; MS in Global Affairs\, NYU SPS Center for Global AffairsPaneli
 sts:Lauren Moss\, Senior Vice President\, Chief Sustainability Officer\, 
 Vornado Realty TrustAnthony L. Perez\, Policy Advisor\, Climate Data and 
 Emissions Specialist\, NYC Mayor's Office of Climate &amp\; Environmental
  JusticeChhavi Maggu\, Senior Sustainability Program Manager\, North Amer
 ica Operations\, AmazonEmma Marshall-Torres\, Regulatory Affairs Manager\
 , Scale MicrogridsSaskia Salak\, Project Manager\, Performance Measuremen
 t and Reporting\, NYSERDA
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the <strong><a href="http://www.sc
 ps.nyu.edu/academics/departments/global-affairs.html" target="_blank" rel
 ="noopener">NYU SPS Center for Global Affairs</a></strong> and the Center
  on Global Energy Policy at Columbia University SIPA's <strong><a href="h
 ttps://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__womeninenergy.energyp
 olicy.columbia.edu_&amp\;d=DwMFaQ&amp\;c=slrrB7dE8n7gBJbeO0g-IQ&amp\;r=2E
 2QVW4SeE5863MOhaARuDwTA4zaZ-gmdzWI3bY66Co&amp\;m=hkGo3aJolAPR36XlSCKKZtJl
 T4dLk8gC2sFymsFxa3qlfLn1Wc5v5cmcNatp7gLN&amp\;s=lngGPTXnK7-8MhGwrQ1jeXWs_
 32wC8QI9snbbWpGKYQ&amp\;e=" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Women in Energ
 y</a></strong> initiative (WIE) for a dynamic conversation on the expandi
 ng career opportunities within the sustainability ecosystem.<br /><br /> 
  The conversations around climate action\, sustainability\, and the futur
 e of work are more relevant than ever. As global efforts to decarbonize a
 ccelerate—and as industries like real estate and finance adapt to chang
 ing policy landscapes\, emerging regulations\, and new technologies—sus
 tainability has become a core driver across nearly every sector.<br /><br
  />  Whether you're exploring entry-level opportunities or seeking to piv
 ot your focus toward a low-carbon future\, this discussion will offer val
 uable insights and practical guidance on how to make a lasting impact in 
 this critical\, rapidly evolving field.<br /><br /></p><p><em>Moderator</
 em>:</p><p><strong>Aida Rodriquez</strong>\, Board Member and Former CEO 
 and CSO\; MS in Global Affairs\, NYU SPS Center for Global Affairs<br /><
 br /><em>Panelists</em>:</p><p><strong>Lauren Moss</strong>\, Senior Vice
  President\, Chief Sustainability Officer\, Vornado Realty Trust</p><p><s
 trong>Anthony L. Perez</strong>\, Policy Advisor\, Climate Data and Emiss
 ions Specialist\, NYC Mayor's Office of Climate &amp\; Environmental Just
 ice</p><p><strong>Chhavi Maggu</strong>\, Senior Sustainability Program M
 anager\, North America Operations\, Amazon</p><p><strong>Emma Marshall-To
 rres</strong>\, Regulatory Affairs Manager\, Scale Microgrids</p><p><stro
 ng>Saskia Salak</strong>\, Project Manager\, Performance Measurement and 
 Reporting\, NYSERDA</p>
