SUMMARY:Disabili-Tea: Disability and Fashion
DESCRIPTION:Fashion is more than what we wear\, it's a way we express our
 selves\, navigate the world\, and advocate for access. In this session\, 
 we will discuss how disability influences style\, design\, and representa
 tion. We'll also discuss adaptive fashion\, accessibility\, identity\, an
 d the ways clothing can reflect lived experiences while challenging tradi
 tional ideas of beauty and inclusion.  **Note on Inclusion and Accessibil
 ity: Our events and initiatives are open to all backgrounds and identitie
 s. It is a priority to make our events inclusive and accessible. For any 
 questions or to notify us of a request\, please email accessibility.inclu
 sion@nyu.edu at least 72 hours before the event.**
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Fashion is more than what we wear\, it'
 s a way we express ourselves\, navigate the world\, and advocate for acce
 ss. In this session\, we will discuss how disability influences style\, d
 esign\, and representation. We'll also discuss adaptive fashion\, accessi
 bility\, identity\, and the ways clothing can reflect lived experiences w
 hile challenging traditional ideas of beauty and inclusion.</p><p>  **Not
 e on Inclusion and Accessibility: Our events and initiatives are open to 
 all backgrounds and identities. It is a priority to make our events inclu
 sive and accessible. For any questions or to notify us of a request\, ple
 ase email accessibility.inclusion@nyu.edu at least 72 hours before the ev
 ent.**</p>
