SUMMARY:K-Friends
DESCRIPTION:Join Our Korean Language Table: Connect\, Practice\, and Buil
 d Community!Hosted by KISO (Korean International Students Organization)\,
  in partnership with the Department of East Asian Studies\, the Korean La
 nguage Table is a semi-monthly gathering that brings together students in
 terested in Korean language and culture with Korean international student
 s for conversation\, cultural exchange\, and community building.Throughou
 t the academic year\, Language Table events provide opportunities for stu
 dents enrolled in Korean language courses as well as anyone interested in
  Korean language and culture to engage in informal conversations with Kor
 ean international students. Whether you are a beginner or an advanced lea
 rner\, these gatherings offer a welcoming space to practice speaking and 
 listening skills in real-world settings.Learn Through Cultural ExchangeLa
 nguage learning extends beyond the classroom. By interacting with native 
 speakers and fellow students\, participants gain valuable cultural insigh
 ts\, improve their communication skills\, and develop a deeper understand
 ing of contemporary Korean culture and everyday life.Build Meaningful Con
 nectionsThe Language Table is more than a language learning opportunity. 
 It's a chance to meet new people\, share experiences\, and form friendshi
 ps across cultures. We hope these conversations foster lasting connection
 s and create a stronger sense of community among students.Event DetailsOp
 en to All: Students of all Korean language proficiency levels\, Korean la
 nguage learners\, and anyone interested in Korean culture are welcome.RSV
 P Encouraged: While walk-ins are welcome\, we encourage participants to R
 SVP so that we can prepare for an enjoyable and engaging experience.This 
 event is presented by KISO and co-sponsored by the Department of East Asi
 an Studies.Hosted by: Department of East Asian StudiesAdditional Informat
 ion can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480790 (https://engag
 e.nyu.edu/event/12480790)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join Our Korean Language Table: Connect\, Pr
 actice\, and Build Community!<br />Hosted by KISO (Korean International S
 tudents Organization)\, in partnership with the Department of East Asian 
 Studies\, the Korean Language Table is a semi-monthly gathering that brin
 gs together students interested in Korean language and culture with Korea
 n international students for conversation\, cultural exchange\, and commu
 nity building.<br />Throughout the academic year\, Language Table events 
 provide opportunities for students enrolled in Korean language courses as
  well as anyone interested in Korean language and culture to engage in in
 formal conversations with Korean international students. Whether you are 
 a beginner or an advanced learner\, these gatherings offer a welcoming sp
 ace to practice speaking and listening skills in real-world settings.<br 
 />Learn Through Cultural Exchange<br />Language learning extends beyond t
 he classroom. By interacting with native speakers and fellow students\, p
 articipants gain valuable cultural insights\, improve their communication
  skills\, and develop a deeper understanding of contemporary Korean cultu
 re and everyday life.<br />Build Meaningful Connections<br />The Language
  Table is more than a language learning opportunity. It's a chance to mee
 t new people\, share experiences\, and form friendships across cultures. 
 We hope these conversations foster lasting connections and create a stron
 ger sense of community among students.<br />Event Details<br />Open to Al
 l: Students of all Korean language proficiency levels\, Korean language l
 earners\, and anyone interested in Korean culture are welcome.<br />RSVP 
 Encouraged: While walk-ins are welcome\, we encourage participants to RSV
 P so that we can prepare for an enjoyable and engaging experience.<br />T
 his event is presented by KISO and co-sponsored by the Department of East
  Asian Studies.<br />Hosted by: Department of East Asian Studies<br />Add
 itional Information can be found at: <a href="https://engage.nyu.edu/even
 t/12480790" target="_blank">https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480790</a>
