DESCRIPTION:Supplemental Learning Groups (SLGs) are lecture specific and 
 give you a chance to practice and test your understanding of the material
  from the past week's lecture(s) in a collaborative group environment. Th
 is is process-based learning\, meaning if you continue to attend\, your l
 earning will compound over the course of the semester. One time attendanc
 e will likely not be very helpful.&#160\;In order for this to be effectiv
 e:- You must come ready to collaborate.- You must come ready to speak.- Y
 ou must be active.&#160\;This will be a framework that you might not be u
 sed to. In this space\, the primary aim is to construct knowledge\, which
  can feel frustrating.Hosted by: University Learning CenterAdditional Inf
 ormation can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12720441 (https://
 engage.nyu.edu/event/12720441)
