LOCATION:LGBTQ+ Center
SUMMARY:Quench: Global LGBTQ+ Experiences
DESCRIPTION:LGBTQ+ experiences vary widely around the world\, shaped by p
 olitical\, religious\, and societal forces. In this Quench\, we'll explor
 e the unique experiences of LGBTQ+ communities across different countries
 \, including places where LGBTQ+ identities and forms of gender expressio
 n are heavily stigmatized. Together\, we'll consider the challenges queer
  and trans people face globally\, as well as the ways they continue to bu
 ild community\, celebrate identity\, and create joy. All are welcome\, an
 d free lunch will be provided!  **Note on Inclusion and Accessibility: Ou
 r events and initiatives are open to all backgrounds and identities. It i
 s a priority to make our events inclusive and accessible. For any questio
 ns or to notify us of a request\, please email lgbtq@nyu.edu (http://nyu.
 edu) at least 72 hours before the event.**
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  LGBTQ+ experiences vary widely around t
 he world\, shaped by political\, religious\, and societal forces. In this
  Quench\, we'll explore the unique experiences of LGBTQ+ communities acro
 ss different countries\, including places where LGBTQ+ identities and for
 ms of gender expression are heavily stigmatized. Together\, we'll conside
 r the challenges queer and trans people face globally\, as well as the wa
 ys they continue to build community\, celebrate identity\, and create joy
 . All are welcome\, and free lunch will be provided!</p><p>  **<em><stron
 g>Note on Inclusion and Accessibility</strong>: Our events and initiative
 s are open to all backgrounds and identities. It is a priority to make ou
 r events inclusive and accessible. For any questions or to notify us of a
  request\, please email lgbtq@<a href="http://nyu.edu" target="_blank" re
 l="noopener nofollow noreferrer">nyu.edu</a> at least 72 hours before the
  event.</em>**</p>
