DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T130000
LOCATION:14A Washington Mews
SUMMARY:When the Horrors of War Meet the Power of Literature: Reactions a
 nd Transformations
DESCRIPTION:This book is an initiative of the The Parents Circle – Fami
 lies Forum (PCFF)\, edited by Sarai Shavit with fellow writer and literar
 y editor Dr. Rawya Burbara. This is a multilingual anthology of short sto
 ries written by authors from both sides of the Israeli-Palestinian divide
 \, addressing how contemporary Arab and Hebrew literature from both sides
  of the fence responds\, clashes\, and evolves in a contemporary geopolit
 ical crisis as war. It tells the complex story of authors who collaborate
 d on a joint artistic project before the war\, and whose personal lives a
 nd creative work changed deeply after October 7th. The anthology offers a
  rare testimony to the power of art and humanity in such harsh and brutal
  times.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This book is an initiative of the The P
 arents Circle – Families Forum (PCFF)\, edited by Sarai Shavit with fel
 low writer and literary editor Dr. Rawya Burbara. This is a multilingual 
 anthology of short stories written by authors from both sides of the Isra
 eli-Palestinian divide\, addressing how contemporary Arab and Hebrew lite
 rature from both sides of the fence responds\, clashes\, and evolves in a
  contemporary geopolitical crisis as war. It tells the complex story of a
 uthors who collaborated on a joint artistic project before the war\, and 
 whose personal lives and creative work changed deeply after October 7th. 
 The anthology offers a rare testimony to the power of art and humanity in
  such harsh and brutal times.</p>
