X-NYU-BRIEFING:This book is
  an initiative of the The Parents Circle – Families Forum (PCFF)\, edit
 ed by Sarai Shavit with fellow writer and literary editor Dr. Rawya Burba
 ra. This is a multilingual anthology of short stories written by authors 
 from both sides of the Israeli-Palestinian divide\, addressing how contem
 porary Arab-Hebrew literature from both sides of the fence responds\, cla
 shes\, and evolves in a contemporary geopolitical crisis as war. It tells
  the complex story of authors who collaborated on a joint artistic projec
 t before the war\, and whose personal lives and creative work changed dee
 ply after October 7th. The anthology offers a rare testimony to the power
  of art and humanity in such harsh and brutal times.\n\n\n\nSarai Sha
 vit is a poet\, author\, and literary editor. She has published two prose
  books and three poetry collections. Her award-winning poetry has been tr
 anslated into Italian\, German\, English\, Portuguese\, and Malayalam. Am
 ong the awards she has won are the Tel Aviv Municipality Poetry Prize and
  The Goldberg Prize for Literature. Her book “Figures of Speech” won 
 the Eddi-Vitz Adeline della Pergola Prize for Translated Literature for 2
 023\, and has been translated into Italian and Portuguese. Shavit teaches
  literature and creative writing at Tel Aviv University and the Universit
 y of Turin.
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
