BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T153000
SUMMARY:CMS 201: Know Your Components
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the CMS 201 Training: Know Your Components\, a ha
 nds-on training session designed for NYU CMS users who are ready to go de
 eper into building and structuring web content. You will get a practical\
 , component-by-component walkthrough of the CMS and leave feeling confide
 nt building pages from scratch.  In This Session  We'll take a deep dive 
 into the full range of CMS components — including the Rich Text Editor\
 , Promo Components\, Image Components\, Tabs\, Expandables\, Big Numbers\
 , and more. For each\, you'll learn what it does\, when to use it\, and h
 ow to add it effectively. We'll also cover how to think strategically abo
 ut page structure\, how to combine components for clarity\, and key best 
 practices around accessibility and design.  Ideal Participant  This sessi
 on is designed for those who have completed CMS 101 and are ready to buil
 d on that foundation. Please note that CMS 101 is a prerequisite for this
  training.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for the CMS 201 Training: Know 
 Your Components\, a hands-on training session designed for NYU CMS users 
 who are ready to go deeper into building and structuring web content. You
  will get a practical\, component-by-component walkthrough of the CMS and
  leave feeling confident building pages from scratch.</p><h2>  In This Se
 ssion</h2><p>  We'll take a deep dive into the full range of CMS componen
 ts — including the Rich Text Editor\, Promo Components\, Image Componen
 ts\, Tabs\, Expandables\, Big Numbers\, and more. For each\, you'll learn
  what it does\, when to use it\, and how to add it effectively. We'll als
 o cover how to think strategically about page structure\, how to combine 
 components for clarity\, and key best practices around accessibility and 
 design.</p><h2>  Ideal Participant</h2><p>  This session is designed for 
 those who have completed CMS 101 and are ready to build on that foundatio
 n. Please note that CMS 101 is a prerequisite for this training.</p>
UID:20261015T180000Z-403627@events.nyu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260908T175835Z
URL:https://events.nyu.edu/event/403627-cms-201-know-your-components
