LOCATION:Dibner Library\, LC 433\, Bern Dibner Library
SUMMARY:Engaging in STEM Scholarly Research: Best Practices for the Schol
 arly Landscape
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is designed for STEM graduate students or upper
  level undergraduates interested in engaging with STEM research.In this w
 orkshop\, we will breakdown the scholarly research landscape to better un
 derstand:how to effectively search and find scholarly materials\,how to d
 etermine where is appropriate to share your own research\, andhow you can
  best make your own work discoverable to your peers.Through a mix of best
  practices and discussion\, attendees will leave this workshop with a bet
 ter understanding of the work of a STEM researcher and with a number of r
 esources to assist them in their own work.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:This workshop is designed for STEM graduate 
 students or upper level undergraduates interested in engaging with STEM r
 esearch.<br />In this workshop\, we will breakdown the scholarly research
  landscape to better understand:<br />how to effectively search and find 
 scholarly materials\,<br />how to determine where is appropriate to share
  your own research\, and<br />how you can best make your own work discove
 rable to your peers.<br />Through a mix of best practices and discussion\
 , attendees will leave this workshop with a better understanding of the w
 ork of a STEM researcher and with a number of resources to assist them in
  their own work.
