DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T200000
LOCATION:19 UP\, Room 101 (Great Room)
GEO:40.73128;-73.9948
SUMMARY:Nihongo Table: Movie Night
DESCRIPTION:Experience Japanese language and culture through film at Niho
 ngo Table: Movie Night! Join fellow students for a screening of a Japanes
 e film followed by casual discussion and cultural exchange in a welcoming
  and supportive environment. Whether you're a beginner or an advanced spe
 aker\, this is a great opportunity to strengthen your listening skills\, 
 learn new vocabulary in context\, and engage with Japanese culture throug
 h cinema. Share your thoughts\, ask questions\, and connect with other Ja
 panese language learners while enjoying a movie together. All language le
 vels are welcome!Who: Japanese language learners of all levels and anyone
  interested in Japanese film\, language\, and culture.Featured Film:&#160
 \;After Life&#160\;(1998)Synopsis:&#160\;In this acclaimed Japanese film\
 , a group of people who have recently died find themselves in a limbo rea
 lm resembling a relatively mundane building. Counselors\, including Takas
 hi (Arata) and Shiori (Erika Oda)\, are on hand to help new arrivals pick
  one memory from their lives to bring with them into eternity. Once the m
 emories are chosen\, the staff makes a short film representing each one\,
  and the films make up a collage of thoughtful cinematic moments.Subtitle
 s will be provided.Hosted by: Department of East Asian StudiesAdditional 
 Information can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480836 (https
 ://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480836)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Experience Japanese language and culture thr
 ough film at Nihongo Table: Movie Night! Join fellow students for a scree
 ning of a Japanese film followed by casual discussion and cultural exchan
 ge in a welcoming and supportive environment. Whether you're a beginner o
 r an advanced speaker\, this is a great opportunity to strengthen your li
 stening skills\, learn new vocabulary in context\, and engage with Japane
 se culture through cinema. Share your thoughts\, ask questions\, and conn
 ect with other Japanese language learners while enjoying a movie together
 . All language levels are welcome!<br />Who: Japanese language learners o
 f all levels and anyone interested in Japanese film\, language\, and cult
 ure.<br />Featured Film:&#160\;After Life&#160\;(1998)<br />Synopsis:&#16
 0\;In this acclaimed Japanese film\, a group of people who have recently 
 died find themselves in a limbo realm resembling a relatively mundane bui
 lding. Counselors\, including Takashi (Arata) and Shiori (Erika Oda)\, ar
 e on hand to help new arrivals pick one memory from their lives to bring 
 with them into eternity. Once the memories are chosen\, the staff makes a
  short film representing each one\, and the films make up a collage of th
 oughtful cinematic moments.<br />Subtitles will be provided.<br />Hosted 
 by: Department of East Asian Studies<br />Additional Information can be f
 ound at: <a href="https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480836" target="_blank">
 https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12480836</a>
