SUMMARY:The Score: Sports Betting's Grip on College Students
DESCRIPTION:NYU Liberal Studies\, NYU Athletics\, and the Office of Stude
 nt-Athlete Excellence are hosting The Score: Sports Betting's Grip on Col
 lege Students\, featuring a conversation with sports business\, law\, and
  society expert\,Kenneth L. Shropshire (https://www.kennethshropshire.com
 /). He will be joined byRyan Westman (https://gonyuathletics.com/staff-di
 rectory/ryan-westman/504)\, NYU's director of academic and student-athlet
 e support services and compliance officer\, andMalik Williams (https://go
 nyuathletics.com/staff-directory/malik-williams/673)(LAW '19)\, NYU's ass
 ociate director of athletics for compliance\, who will act as moderators.
 This discussion will draw on perspectives from scholarship\, sports compe
 tition\, law\, and business. They will explore how sports betting has bec
 ome rampant—including who is impacted\, who benefits\, and insights on 
 the way forward.Doors Open at 5:30 p.m. Program will be 6:00–7:30 p.m. 
 Refreshments will be served.Open to the NYU community and the general pub
 lic. Visitors must RSVP in advance and have a valid government ID to ente
 r the building.RSVP Below to AttendAbout Kenneth L. ShropshireKenneth L. 
 Shropshire (https://www.kennethshropshire.com/) is the David W. Hauck Pro
 fessor Emeritus of Legal Studies and Business Ethics at the Wharton Schoo
 l of the University of Pennsylvania and Professor Emeritus of Africana St
 udies. His scholarship and professional work explore the intersections of
  sports business\, law\, and race\, as well as the opportunities and resp
 onsibilities educational institutions have toward athletes.              
 He is the coauthor\, with Collin D. Williams\, Jr.\, of The Miseducation 
 of the Student-Athlete: How to Fix College Sports\, recently reissued wit
 h a new preface examining the evolving landscape of college athletics. Hi
 s other related books include In Black and White\, Sport Matters\, and Th
 e Business of Sports Agents.              Shropshire founded the Wharton 
 Sports Business Initiative and later established and led the Global Sport
  Institute at Arizona State University. He currently serves as a Strategi
 c Advisor to SeventySix Capital and as Lead Independent Director of Moeli
 s &amp\; Company. A graduate of Stanford University and Columbia Law Scho
 ol\, he began his career in private law practice and later worked with th
 e Los Angeles Olympic Organizing Committee.      About Ryan WestmanRyan W
 estman (https://gonyuathletics.com/staff-directory/ryan-westman/504) serv
 es as Director of Academic and Student-Athlete Support Services at New Yo
 rk University\, where he supports the academic\, leadership\, and persona
 l development of student-athletes and serves as sport advisor for basebal
 l\, wrestling\, and men's and women's cross country and track &amp\; fiel
 d.              He joined NYU in 2018 after nearly seven years at Seton H
 all University\, where he advised student-athletes across multiple sports
  and served as a mentor in the Freshman Studies Program.              Out
 side of his administrative work at NYU\, Westman teaches courses on Inter
 collegiate Athletics at NYU Steinhardt in the Higher Education and Studen
 t Affairs (HESA) program and in the School of Professional Studies (SPS) 
 Sports Business program.              A 2006 graduate of Rutgers Universi
 ty\, Westman competed in track &amp\; field for four years and served as 
 a captain of the program's first BIG EAST and IC4A championship teams. He
  was inducted into the Rutgers Athletics Hall of Fame in 2017. Westman ea
 rned his Ph.D. in Higher Education Leadership\, Management and Policy fro
 m Seton Hall University in 2018. His doctoral research examined the impac
 t of NCAA policies and programs on Historically Black Colleges and Univer
 sities (HBCUs) and Limited Resource Institutions competing in Division I 
 athletics.      About Malik WilliamsMalik Williams (https://gonyuathletic
 s.com/staff-directory/malik-williams/673)&#160\;is in his fourth year as 
 an Associate Director of Athletics at New York University. Malik plays a 
 key role in the Department's strategic and financial planning while overs
 eeing its NCAA compliance operation. He also provides sport oversight for
  several varsity programs: Men's Basketball\, Men's and Women's Swimming\
 , Men's and Women's Cross Country/Track &amp\; Field\, and Baseball.     
          Prior to joining NYU Athletics\, Malik worked as an Associate At
 torney at Winston &amp\; Strawn LLP in the firm's Antitrust and Sports Li
 tigation practice. During his time at Winston\, he represented a number o
 f high-profile clients\, including Ben Simmons\, Division I student-athle
 tes\, the NFL Players Association\, Relevant Sports Group\, and Activisio
 n Blizzard.              Malik is an alumnus of NYU School of Law\, where
  he earned his J.D. in May 2019.        &#160\;Note on Accessibility: It 
 is a priority to make our events inclusive and accessible. The entrance o
 f 708 Broadway and the 3rd Floor are accessible via elevator. For any que
 stions or to notify us of accommodation requests\, please emaillsdeansoff
 ice@nyu.eduat least two weeks prior to the event date.
