LOCATION:Global Center for Academic and Spiritual Life\; Suite 491
GEO:40.7299;-73.9982
SUMMARY:Modern Connection: Student Dinner with Casper ter Kuile
DESCRIPTION:Building deep and meaningful friendships feels more complicat
 ed than ever. If you're looking for practical ways to strengthen your rel
 ationships while you juggle competing demands\, join us for dinner and a 
 discussion with Casper ter Kuile\, author of The Power of Ritual (https:/
 /www.harpercollins.com/products/the-power-of-ritual-casper-ter-kuile?vari
 ant=32894732140578) and GSL Scholar-in-Residence. You'll be empowered to 
 show up in the ways that matter to you\, whether you're asking how to be 
 a better friend\, partner\, student\, or professional. Casper is a leadin
 g scholar of ritual\, relationship\, and modern spirituality\, exploring 
 the relational practices that apply to all belief systems and backgrounds
   Dinner will be provided. Please note that this gathering is intended fo
 r undergraduate and graduate students at NYU.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Building deep and meaningful friendship
 s feels more complicated than ever. If you're looking for practical ways 
 to strengthen your relationships while you juggle competing demands\, joi
 n us for dinner and a discussion with Casper ter Kuile\, author of <em><a
  href="https://www.harpercollins.com/products/the-power-of-ritual-casper-
 ter-kuile?variant=32894732140578">The Power of Ritual</a></em> and GSL Sc
 holar-in-Residence. You'll be empowered to show up in the ways that matte
 r to you\, whether you're asking how to be a better friend\, partner\, st
 udent\, or professional. Casper is a leading scholar of ritual\, relation
 ship\, and modern spirituality\, exploring the relational practices that 
 apply to all belief systems and backgrounds</p><p>  Dinner will be provid
 ed. Please note that this gathering is intended for undergraduate and gra
 duate students at NYU.</p>
