DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T210000
LOCATION:James Earl Jones Theatre
GEO:40.75916;-73.983055
SUMMARY:WANTED
DESCRIPTION:How far would you go to get everything you ever WANTED?  Texa
 s\, 1893 — Twin sisters Mary and Martha Clarke are on the run. The sist
 ers\, Black women who pass for white and hide in plain sight\, straddle a
  dangerous line between two Americas. But as powerful forces close in to 
 keep their family from claiming a future of their own\, Mary and Martha a
 re driven to desperate measures to save their mother and their family's l
 egacy. When survival demands they do the unthinkable\, the sisters nevert
 heless fight for self-determination\, dignity\, and the inheritance they 
 have long been denied.  A soulful and dangerous new Broadway musical\, WA
 NTED is the mostly true story of Mary and Martha Clarke: sisters\, outlaw
 s\, legends. This New York Times Critic's Pick has been hailed as "thrill
 ingly original" with an "audacious and rollicking story." The production 
 stars Solea Pfeiffer as Mary\, Liisi LaFontaine as Martha\, and Grammy® 
 Award winner Ledisi as Tallulah. The Kinfolk\, a vibrant chorus of ancest
 ors\, guide them forward on an odyssey of sisterhood\, rebellion\, and fr
 eedom.WANTED features book and lyrics by Variety "Star to Watch" Angelica
  Chéri\, a descendant of the Sisters Clarke\, and music by Richard Rodge
 rs Award–winning composer Ross Baum. The production is directed by Tony
  Award® nominee and Obie Award® winner Stevie Walker-Webb\, with choreo
 graphy by Chelsey Arce.                  &#160\;                On sale N
 OW through NYUHome!How to Purchase Tickets Online (http://www.nyu.edu/lif
 e/resources-and-services/nyu-box-office/ticket-central/faqs/online-orderi
 ng-faq.html)YOU MUST PRESENT YOUR NYU ID AND THE CREDIT CARD YOU WILL BE 
 USING TO PURCHASE THESE TICKETS AT NYU BOX OFFICE IN ORDER TO CLAIM YOUR 
 TICKETS.                  Check your purchase confirmation email for spec
 ific information regarding ticket pick-up. Box office hours are Tuesday-S
 aturday\, 12pm-6pm. Closed on most university holidays and breaks. Summer
  hours vary. Check our website (https://www.nyu.edu/life/resources-and-se
 rvices/nyu-box-office.html) for more details                DO NOT ATTEMP
 T TO PICK UP YOUR TICKETS AT THE VENUE. There are no refunds or exchanges
  on these tickets.                                  THERE IS A LIMIT OF 4
  TICKETS PER NYU ID for most events. For specific ticket limit informatio
 n\, check the information above. Multiple orders by the same person/ID/cr
 edit card will be cancelled and tickets will be resold.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Z
 IPUX7JD4u4?si=P4v22kccOgrZ9wxe&amp\;wmode=transparent" title="YouTube vid
 eo player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer\; autoplay\; clipboard-wr
 ite\; encrypted-media\; gyroscope\; picture-in-picture\; web-share" refer
 rerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen="" style="wid
 th: 566px\; height: 318px\;" class="lw_media lw_media_responsive"></ifram
 e><p class="p1" style="text-align: center\;">  How far would you go to ge
 t everything you ever <em>WANTED</em>?</p><p class="p1" style="text-align
 : center\;">  Texas\, 1893 — Twin sisters Mary and Martha Clarke are on
  the run. The sisters\, Black women who pass for white and hide in plain 
 sight\, straddle a dangerous line between two Americas. But as powerful f
 orces close in to keep their family from claiming a future of their own\,
  Mary and Martha are driven to desperate measures to save their mother an
 d their family's legacy. When survival demands they do the unthinkable\, 
 the sisters nevertheless fight for self-determination\, dignity\, and the
  inheritance they have long been denied.</p><p class="p1" style="text-ali
 gn: center\;">  A soulful and dangerous new Broadway musical\, <em>WANTED
 </em> is the mostly true story of Mary and Martha Clarke: sisters\, outla
 ws\, legends. This <em>New York Times</em> Critic's Pick has been hailed 
 as "thrillingly original" with an "audacious and rollicking story." The p
 roduction stars Solea Pfeiffer as Mary\, Liisi LaFontaine as Martha\, and
  Grammy<sup>®</sup> Award winner Ledisi as Tallulah. The Kinfolk\, a vib
 rant chorus of ancestors\, guide them forward on an odyssey of sisterhood
 \, rebellion\, and freedom.</p><p class="p1" style="text-align: center\;"
 ><em>WANTED</em> features book and lyrics by Variety "Star to Watch" Ange
 lica Chéri\, a descendant of the Sisters Clarke\, and music by Richard R
 odgers Award–winning composer Ross Baum. The production is directed by 
 Tony Award<sup>®</sup> nominee and Obie Award<sup>®</sup> winner Stevie
  Walker-Webb\, with choreography by Chelsey Arce.</p><div class="content-
 row row"><div class="content-column col-md-12 content-column--last"><div 
 class="content-column__inner"><div class="column-text"><div class="conten
 t-row row"><div class="content-column col-md-12 content-column--last"><di
 v class="content-column__inner"><div class="column-text"><p style="text-a
 lign: center\;">                  &#160\;                </p><p style="te
 xt-align: center\;" align="center"><strong><em>On sale NOW through NYUHom
 e!<br /></em></strong></p><p style="text-align: center\;" align="center">
 <strong><em><a href="http://www.nyu.edu/life/resources-and-services/nyu-b
 ox-office/ticket-central/faqs/online-ordering-faq.html">How to Purchase T
 ickets Online</a></em></strong></p><p style="text-align: center\;"><stron
 g>YOU MUST PRESENT YOUR NYU ID AND THE CREDIT CARD YOU WILL BE USING TO P
 URCHASE THESE TICKETS AT NYU BOX OFFICE IN ORDER TO CLAIM YOUR TICKETS.</
 strong></p><p style="text-align: center\;">                  Check your p
 urchase confirmation email for specific information regarding ticket pick
 -up. Box office hours are Tuesday-Saturday\, 12pm-6pm. Closed on most uni
 versity holidays and breaks. Summer hours vary. Check our <a href="https:
 //www.nyu.edu/life/resources-and-services/nyu-box-office.html" target="_b
 lank" rel="noopener noreferrer">website</a> for more details             
    </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>DO NOT ATTEMPT TO PICK UP 
 YOUR TICKETS AT THE VENUE.</strong> There are no refunds or exchanges on 
 these tickets.                </p><p style="text-align: center\;">       
            THERE IS A LIMIT OF 4 TICKETS PER NYU ID for most events. For 
 specific ticket limit information\, check the information above. Multiple
  orders by the same person/ID/credit card will be cancelled and tickets w
 ill be resold.                </p></div></div></div></div></div></div></d
