DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T153000
LOCATION:Global Center for Academic and Spiritual Life\; Suite 491
GEO:40.7299;-73.9982
SUMMARY:Dharma for Real Life: What am I supposed to do with my life?
DESCRIPTION:What am I supposed to do with my life?  The question that kee
 ps you awake at night\, leaving you feeling shaken and unsure. If you're 
 grappling with the answer\, join us for lunch and a panel discussion to e
 xplore how the wisdom of Dharmic traditions can guide you. Our panel of s
 piritual life advisors will talk through how you can approach this big qu
 estion\, both practically and spiritually\, without having to pretend or 
 perform. Leave the evening with a grounded approach to guide you\, regard
 less of your tradition or background.  Lunch will be provided. Open to al
 l members of the NYU community.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  What am I supposed to do with my life?<
 /p><p>  The question that keeps you awake at night\, leaving you feeling 
 shaken and unsure. If you're grappling with the answer\, join us for lunc
 h and a panel discussion to explore how the wisdom of Dharmic traditions 
 can guide you. Our panel of spiritual life advisors will talk through how
  you can approach this big question\, both practically and spiritually\, 
 without having to pretend or perform. Leave the evening with a grounded a
 pproach to guide you\, regardless of your tradition or background.</p><p>
   Lunch will be provided. Open to all members of the NYU community.</p>
UID:20261016T180000Z-406374@events.nyu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260925T094910Z
