GEO:40.72861;-73.99195
SUMMARY:Food Forests and Foraging
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a conversation with Zoe Yang\, forager\, w
 riter\, and recipe developer who has written for publications such as Bon
  Appetit\, Grist\, and Mala Market on topics ranging from food as protest
  to how to wind cure a duck. We will talk about mycorrhizal relationships
  of fungi with native trees\, soil health\, seasonality\, plant medicine\
 , and how to forage ethically in an urban environment\, including food fo
 rests.Hosted by: Mycology Group at NYU - All-UniversityAdditional Informa
 tion can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12867381 (https://enga
 ge.nyu.edu/event/12867381)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Please join us for a conversation with Zoe Y
 ang\, forager\, writer\, and recipe developer who has written for publica
 tions such as Bon Appetit\, Grist\, and Mala Market on topics ranging fro
 m food as protest to how to wind cure a duck. We will talk about mycorrhi
 zal relationships of fungi with native trees\, soil health\, seasonality\
 , plant medicine\, and how to forage ethically in an urban environment\, 
 including food forests.<br />Hosted by: Mycology Group at NYU - All-Unive
 rsity<br />Additional Information can be found at: <a href="https://engag
 e.nyu.edu/event/12867381" target="_blank">https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12
 867381</a>
