SUMMARY:Translation Lecture Series: Translation and Justice in Socio-Envi
 ronmental Conflicts
DESCRIPTION:How can translators help co-create knowledge across communiti
 es and help broaden participation in climate justice processes? What goes
  into scientific and technical translation beyond knowledge of language a
 nd science? Is translation only a transfer of such knowledge or is it als
 o a world-making practice? How can translators and researchers resist env
 ironmental injustice in and with communities that face the most impact? D
 rawing from her ethnographic research and her own practice\, Piñeiro exa
 mines how translators and interpreters can use their research\, language\
 , and intercultural skills to be important allies in the work of environm
 ental justice.  Sponsored by Critical Creative Production (https://libera
 lstudies.nyu.edu/academics/gls-curriculum/concentrations/critical-creativ
 e-production.html?challenge=d06e90d7-4d8f-4b88-9d8c-10b73beb60f1) and the
  Minor in Translation Studies (https://liberalstudies.nyu.edu/academics/m
 inor-in-translation-studies.html?challenge=d06e90d7-4d8f-4b88-9d8c-10b73b
 eb60f1)\, with support from the LS Programming and Events Committee. Refr
 eshments will be served.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  How can translators help co-create know
 ledge across communities and help broaden participation in climate justic
 e processes? What goes into scientific and technical translation beyond k
 nowledge of language and science? Is translation only a transfer of such 
 knowledge or is it also a world-making practice? How can translators and 
 researchers resist environmental injustice in and with communities that f
 ace the most impact? Drawing from her ethnographic research and her own p
 ractice\, Piñeiro examines how translators and interpreters can use thei
 r research\, language\, and intercultural skills to be important allies i
 n the work of environmental justice.</p><p>  Sponsored by <a href="https:
 //liberalstudies.nyu.edu/academics/gls-curriculum/concentrations/critical
 -creative-production.html?challenge=d06e90d7-4d8f-4b88-9d8c-10b73beb60f1"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Critical Creative Production</a> and the 
 <a href="https://liberalstudies.nyu.edu/academics/minor-in-translation-st
 udies.html?challenge=d06e90d7-4d8f-4b88-9d8c-10b73beb60f1" target="_blank
 " rel="noopener">Minor in Translation Studies</a>\, with support from the
  LS Programming and Events Committee. Refreshments will be served.&#160\;
 </p>
