SUMMARY:The Art of Uncertainty Series: The Practice of Uncertainty
DESCRIPTION:Most of us were never taught to sit with not knowing.We were 
 taught to solve\, fix\, scroll\, or distract ourselves. But what if uncer
 tainty isn't a problem to eliminate\, but a skill to practice?Join us for
  a 3-part conversation series exploring:The Pain of Uncertainty (9/22)The
  Practice of Uncertainty (10/20)Learning from Uncertainty (11/17)Where: G
 CASL 475Time: 12:00–1:00 p.m. (ET)Together we'll reflect on boredom\, c
 ompulsion\, relief-seeking\, and how to imagine new ways of being.Open to
  all students navigating stress\, big questions\, habits\, or distraction
 . Come to one session or join them all!&#160\;No lectures\, just shared e
 xploration.Co-hosted by the NYU Collegiate Recovery Program\, Student Wel
 lbeing\, and Global Spiritual Life.&#160\;&#160\;Hosted by: NYU Student W
 ellbeingAdditional Information can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/ev
 ent/12777796 (https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12777796)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Most of us were never taught to sit with not
  knowing.<br />We were taught to solve\, fix\, scroll\, or distract ourse
 lves. But what if uncertainty isn't a problem to eliminate\, but a skill 
 to practice?<br />Join us for a 3-part conversation series exploring:<br 
 />The Pain of Uncertainty (9/22)<br />The Practice of Uncertainty (10/20)
