LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 7th Floor\, Rm. 745\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Mindfulness Moment at Bobst
DESCRIPTION:"Breath is the bridge which connects life to consciousness\, 
 which unites your body to your thoughts. Whenever your mind becomes scatt
 ered\, use your breath as the means to take hold of your mind again." - T
 hich Nhat HanhTake a mindfulness moment and join us in community for a se
 ries of 30-minute meditation sessions where we will explore the practice 
 of meditation. Our practice this semester will be centered on using objec
 ts: plants\, tea\, rocks\, as a point of focus and contemplation. The ses
 sions will offer you techniques that will help you to center yourself to 
 stay focused and grounded as you navigate through the semester.These sess
 ions are part of an ongoing series of community meditations that will hap
 pen throughout the semester. Please check the Library Events calendar for
  our upcoming sessions. Registration appreciated\, walk-ins welcome.NYU L
 ibraries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individua
 ls with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email
  lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's 
 campuses and facilities.
