  consciousness\, which unites your body to your thoughts. Whenever your m
 ind becomes scattered\, use your breath as the means to take hold of your
  mind again." - Thich Nhat Hanh<br />Take a mindfulness moment and join u
 s in community for a series of 30-minute meditation sessions where we wil
 l explore the practice of meditation. Our practice this semester will be 
 centered on using objects: plants\, tea\, rocks\, as a point of focus and
  contemplation. The sessions will offer you techniques that will help you
  to center yourself to stay focused and grounded as you navigate through 
 the semester.<br />These sessions are part of an ongoing series of commun
 ity meditations that will happen throughout the semester. Please check th
 e Library Events calendar for our upcoming sessions. Registration appreci
 ated\, walk-ins welcome.<br />NYU Libraries is committed to providing rea
 sonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you have an a
 ccommodation request\, please email lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\,
  masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
