SUMMARY:2026 Henry Hart Rice Urban Policy Forum
DESCRIPTION:Join the NYU Wagner community for the Henry Hart Rice Urban P
 olicy Forum\, an annual engagement in which public service leaders examin
 e the most critical issues in policy and city planning. This year\, we ar
 e honored to have Christina Greer in conversation with Mitchell Moss\, th
 e Henry Hart Rice Professor of Urban Policy and Planning\, to discuss pub
 lic policy and urban politics.Christina Greer is a Professor of Political
  Science at Fordham University and an expert on urban politics and race. 
 She is the author of Black Politics in Transition: Immigration\, Suburban
 ization and Gentrification\, and How to Build a Democracy: From Fannie Lo
 u Hamer and Barbara Jordan to Stacey Abrams\, and the co-editor of Black 
 Ethnics: Race\, Immigration and the Pursuit of the American Dream. Profes
 sor Greer is the inaugural Senior Policy Fellow at the Brooklyn Organizat
 ion and the co-host of the podcast\, FAQ: NYC.This event is for all NYU s
 tudents\, staff\, faculty\, and members of the broader community. The doo
 rs will open at 5:45pm.RSVP: https://wagner.nyu.edu/community/events/2026
 -henry-hart-rice-urban-policy-forum-2026-10-20 (https://wagner.nyu.edu/co
 mmunity/events/2026-henry-hart-rice-urban-policy-forum-2026-10-20)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join the NYU Wagner community for the Henry 
 Hart Rice Urban Policy Forum\, an annual engagement in which public servi
 ce leaders examine the most critical issues in policy and city planning. 
 This year\, we are honored to have Christina Greer in conversation with M
 itchell Moss\, the Henry Hart Rice Professor of Urban Policy and Planning
 \, to discuss public policy and urban politics.<br />Christina Greer is a
  Professor of Political Science at Fordham University and an expert on ur
 ban politics and race. She is the author of Black Politics in Transition:
  Immigration\, Suburbanization and Gentrification\, and How to Build a De
 mocracy: From Fannie Lou Hamer and Barbara Jordan to Stacey Abrams\, and 
 the co-editor of Black Ethnics: Race\, Immigration and the Pursuit of the
  American Dream. Professor Greer is the inaugural Senior Policy Fellow at
  the Brooklyn Organization and the co-host of the podcast\, FAQ: NYC.<br 
 /><strong>This event is for all NYU students\, staff\, faculty\, and memb
 ers of the broader community. The doors will open at 5:45pm.</strong><br 
