SUMMARY:The Outsiders
DESCRIPTION:In Tulsa\, Oklahoma\, 1967\, the hardened hearts and aching s
 ouls of Ponyboy Curtis\, Johnny Cade and their chosen family of 'outsider
 s' are in a fight for survival and a quest for purpose in a world that ma
 y never accept them. A story of the bonds that brothers share and the hop
 es we all hold on to\, this gripping new musical reinvigorates the timele
 ss tale of 'haves and have nots'\, of protecting what's yours and fightin
 g for what could be.On sale NOW through NYUHome!How to Purchase Tickets O
 nline (http://www.nyu.edu/life/resources-and-services/nyu-box-office/tick
 et-central/faqs/online-ordering-faq.html)YOU MUST PRESENT YOUR NYU ID AND
  THE CREDIT CARD YOU WILL BE USING TO PURCHASE THESE TICKETS AT NYU BOX O
 FFICE IN ORDER TO CLAIM YOUR TICKETS.                  Check your purchas
 e confirmation email for specific information regarding ticket pick-up. B
 ox office hours are Tuesday-Saturday\, 12pm-6pm. Closed on most universit
 y holidays and breaks. Summer hours vary. Check our website (https://www.
 nyu.edu/life/resources-and-services/nyu-box-office.html) for more details
                 DO NOT ATTEMPT TO PICK UP YOUR TICKETS AT THE VENUE. Ther
 e are no refunds or exchanges on these tickets.                          
         THERE IS A LIMIT OF 4 TICKETS PER NYU ID for most events. For spe
 cific ticket limit information\, check the information above. Multiple or
 ders by the same person/ID/credit card will be cancelled and tickets will
  be resold.
