LOCATION:Room N107
SUMMARY:Science\, the Humanities\, and Our Lives: Facing the Age of AI
DESCRIPTION:Program:Opening Remarks by NYU Shanghai Provost Bei Wu (5 min
 utes)  Professor Ge Jianxiong's Keynote: "Science\, the Humanities\, and 
 Our Lives: Navigating the Age of AI" (45 minutes)  A conversation between
  NYU Shanghai Chancellor Tong Shijun and Professor Ge Jianxiong (30 minut
 es)  Q&amp\;A (10 minutes)  Speaker Bio:  Professor Ge Jianxiong traces h
 is ancestral roots to Shaoxing\, Zhejiang Province. He holds a PhD in His
 tory and is the Library Director of The Chinese University of Hong Kong\,
  Shenzhen\; a Distinguished Senior Professor in the humanities and social
  sciences at Fudan University\; a member of the History Division of the M
 inistry of Education's Social Sciences Committee\; an advisory member of 
 the National Social Science Fund's disciplinary office\; and a Fellow of 
 the Central Research Institute of Culture and History.  Professor Ge prev
 iously served as Director of Fudan University's Institute of Chinese Hist
 orical Geography and Director of its Research Center for Historical Geogr
 aphy\, a Key Research Institute of the Ministry of Education. He has also
  served as Deputy Chair of the Ministry of Education's Committee on Acade
 mic Integrity\; Chair of the Historical Geography Committee of the Geogra
 phical Society of China\; Vice President of the Society for Qin and Han H
 istory Studies\; a council member of the Chinese Historical Society\; Vic
 e President of the Shanghai Historical Society and the Shanghai Society f
 or Social Science Popularization\; and a counselor to the Shanghai Munici
 pal Government. He was a member of the Standing Committee of the 12th Nat
 ional Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference
 .  From 2007 to 2014\, he served as Library Director of Fudan University.
  During that period\, he was also Deputy Chair of the Ministry of Educati
 on's Steering Committee for Academic Libraries and Vice President of the 
 Shanghai Branch of the Library Society of China.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Program:</strong></p><ul><li>Open
 ing Remarks by NYU Shanghai Provost Bei Wu (5 minutes)  </li><li>Professo
 r Ge Jianxiong's Keynote: "Science\, the Humanities\, and Our Lives: Navi
 gating the Age of AI" (45 minutes)  </li><li>A conversation between NYU S
 hanghai Chancellor Tong Shijun and Professor Ge Jianxiong (30 minutes)  <
 /li><li>Q&amp\;A (10 minutes)  </li></ul><p><strong>Speaker Bio:</strong>
 </p><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Professor Ge Jianxiong traces his ancestr
 al roots to Shaoxing\, Zhejiang Province. He holds a PhD in History and i
 s the Library Director of The Chinese University of Hong Kong\, Shenzhen\
 ; a Distinguished Senior Professor in the humanities and social sciences 
 at Fudan University\; a member of the History Division of the Ministry of
  Education's Social Sciences Committee\; an advisory member of the Nation
 al Social Science Fund's disciplinary office\; and a Fellow of the Centra
 l Research Institute of Culture and History.<br /></p><p>  Professor Ge p
 reviously served as Director of Fudan University's Institute of Chinese H
 istorical Geography and Director of its Research Center for Historical Ge
 ography\, a Key Research Institute of the Ministry of Education. He has a
 lso served as Deputy Chair of the Ministry of Education's Committee on Ac
 ademic Integrity\; Chair of the Historical Geography Committee of the Geo
 graphical Society of China\; Vice President of the Society for Qin and Ha
 n History Studies\; a council member of the Chinese Historical Society\; 
 Vice President of the Shanghai Historical Society and the Shanghai Societ
 y for Social Science Popularization\; and a counselor to the Shanghai Mun
 icipal Government. He was a member of the Standing Committee of the 12th 
 National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Confere
 nce.<br /></p><p>  From 2007 to 2014\, he served as Library Director of F
 udan University. During that period\, he was also Deputy Chair of the Min
 istry of Education's Steering Committee for Academic Libraries and Vice P
 resident of the Shanghai Branch of the Library Society of China.<br /></p
