SUMMARY:Civil Discourse Principles and Practice Workshop with the Berkley
  Institute
DESCRIPTION:This hands-on\, practical workshop hosted by the Berkley Inst
 itute (http://nyuberkleyinstitute.org) is designed to equip NYU community
  members with the essential tools needed to navigate charged conversation
 s with confidence\, empathy\, and clarity.  The workshop will focus on bu
 ilding participants' capacity to listen actively\, de-escalate tensions\,
  ask better questions\, and find commonalities over compromise.  All work
 shop participants will be eligible to submit a grant application to the B
 erkley Institute's Community Fund (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAI
 pQLSd5GFQQCYOdxAk9_ZmOGOgZ8552IscQbvgm38zdGF4ju37Jxg/viewform?usp=dialog)
 . Using the skills from the workshop\, participants can create an event o
 f their own that furthers the work of civil discourse at NYU.  Light lunc
 h will be served.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-path-to-node="1">  This hands-on\, p
 ractical workshop hosted by the <a href="http://nyuberkleyinstitute.org" 
 target="_blank" rel="noopener">Berkley Institute</a> is designed to equip
  NYU community members with the essential tools needed to navigate charge
 d conversations with confidence\, empathy\, and clarity.</p><p data-path-
 to-node="2">  The workshop will focus on building participants' capacity 
 to listen actively\, de-escalate tensions\, ask better questions\, and fi
 nd commonalities over compromise.</p><p data-path-to-node="2">  All works
 hop participants will be eligible to submit a grant application to the Be
 rkley Institute's <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd5GF
 QQCYOdxAk9_ZmOGOgZ8552IscQbvgm38zdGF4ju37Jxg/viewform?usp=dialog" target=
 "_blank" rel="noopener">Community Fund</a>. Using the skills from the wor
 kshop\, participants can create an event of their own that furthers the w
 ork of civil discourse at NYU.</p><p data-path-to-node="2">  Light lunch 
 will be served.</p>
