DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T133000
SUMMARY:Is it time to merge?
DESCRIPTION:Right now\, many nonprofits are making hard choices about how
  to sustain their missions in the face of funding cuts and a changed fund
 ing environment. For some\, that means considering whether a merger or co
 llaborative venture could protect programs\, preserve community relations
 hips\, and create a more durable path forward. In this panel\, we'll talk
  candidly about what leads organizations to explore these options\, what 
 concerns or misconceptions can make the conversations difficult\, and how
  leaders can approach the process with clarity\, care\, and a focus on wh
 at the community needs most.  In this session\, we will explore:  - Why m
 ergers and collaborative ventures matter now  - Common challenges and mis
 conceptions  - What becomes possible when shared resources are aligned  -
  Tools for getting startedEvent series: Tough but important conversations
  shaping the future of the nonprofit sector  Nonprofit work is changing\,
  and leaders need space to ask the questions that do not always have easy
  answers. This event series creates room for candid\, thoughtful conversa
 tions about how nonprofits can adapt\, collaborate\, and build stronger p
 aths toward mission impact. Together\, we will explore the challenges\, o
 pportunities\, and new ideas shaping the future of our work and what nonp
 rofit leaders can do now to prepare for what comes next.This event series
  is offered in collaboration with theGeorge H. Heyman\, Jr. Program for P
 hilanthropy and Fundraisingwithin theNYU SPS Center for Global Affairs.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Right now\, many nonprofits are making 
 hard choices about how to sustain their missions in the face of funding c
 uts and a changed funding environment. For some\, that means considering 
 whether a merger or collaborative venture could protect programs\, preser
 ve community relationships\, and create a more durable path forward. In t
 his panel\, we'll talk candidly about what leads organizations to explore
  these options\, what concerns or misconceptions can make the conversatio
 ns difficult\, and how leaders can approach the process with clarity\, ca
 re\, and a focus on what the community needs most.</p><p>  In this sessio
 n\, we will explore:</p><p>  - Why mergers and collaborative ventures mat
 ter now</p><p>  - Common challenges and misconceptions</p><p>  - What bec
 omes possible when shared resources are aligned</p><p>  - Tools for getti
 ng started<br /><br /><strong>Event series: Tough but important conversat
 ions shaping the future of the nonprofit sector</strong></p><p>  Nonprofi
 t work is changing\, and leaders need space to ask the questions that do 
 not always have easy answers. This event series creates room for candid\,
  thoughtful conversations about how nonprofits can adapt\, collaborate\, 
 and build stronger paths toward mission impact. Together\, we will explor
 e the challenges\, opportunities\, and new ideas shaping the future of ou
 r work and what nonprofit leaders can do now to prepare for what comes ne
 xt.</p><p><em>This event series is offered in collaboration with the</em>
 <a href="https://www.sps.nyu.edu/homepage/academics/divisions-and-departm
 ents/center-for-global-affairs/the-george-h-heyman-jr-program-for-philant
 hropy-and-fundraising.html" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"><em>G
 eorge H. Heyman\, Jr. Program for Philanthropy and Fundraising</em></a><e
 m>within the</em><a href="https://www.sps.nyu.edu/homepage/academics/divi
 sions-and-departments/center-for-global-affairs.html" target="_blank" rel
 ="nofollow noopener"><em>NYU SPS Center for Global Affairs</em></a><em>.<
 /em></p>
