LOCATION:Bobst Library\, 7th Floor\, Rm. 745\, Bobst Library
SUMMARY:Meditations on Earth
DESCRIPTION:Guided meditations led by Bart van Melik that weave mindfulne
 ss with reflections on our environment. Explore themes such as the connec
 tedness of all things\, and how we live in relationship with ourselves\, 
 others and the world around us. Delve into the nature of change\, from th
 e expansion of the universe\, the climate\, to the nature of thought itse
 lf.Whether this is your very first meditation\, or are a longtime practit
 ioner\, all are welcome.Cushions\, benches\, chairs\, and backjacks are a
 vailable. Registration is not required but encouraged.Sessions are part o
 f an ongoing community meditation series hosted by the Office of Sustaina
 bility and NYU Libraries on Wednesdays throughout the academic year.NYU L
 ibraries is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individua
 ls with disabilities. If you have an accommodation request\, please email
  lib-reference@nyu.edu. Additionally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's 
 campuses and facilities.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Guided meditations led by Bart van Melik tha
 t weave mindfulness with reflections on our environment. Explore themes s
 uch as the connectedness of all things\, and how we live in relationship 
 with ourselves\, others and the world around us. Delve into the nature of
  change\, from the expansion of the universe\, the climate\, to the natur
 e of thought itself.<br />Whether this is your very first meditation\, or
  are a longtime practitioner\, all are welcome.<br />Cushions\, benches\,
  chairs\, and backjacks are available. Registration is not required but e
 ncouraged.<br />Sessions are part of an ongoing community meditation seri
 es hosted by the Office of Sustainability and NYU Libraries on Wednesdays
  throughout the academic year.<br />NYU Libraries is committed to providi
 ng reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you hav
 e an accommodation request\, please email lib-reference@nyu.edu. Addition
 ally\, masks are always welcome on NYU's campuses and facilities.
