SUMMARY:Supplemental Learning Group - Math for Economics I (Sanfratello)
DESCRIPTION:Supplemental Learning Groups (SLGs) are lecture specific and 
 give you a chance to practice and test your understanding of the material
  from the past week's lecture(s) in a collaborative group environment. Th
 is is process-based learning\, meaning if you continue to attend\, your l
 earning will compound over the course of the semester. One time attendanc
 e will likely not be very helpful.In order for this to be effective:- You
  must come ready to collaborate.- You must come ready to speak.- You must
  be active.This will be a framework that you might not be used to. In thi
 s space\, the primary aim is to construct knowledge\, which can feel frus
 trating.Hosted by: University Learning CenterAdditional Information can b
 e found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12720048 (https://engage.nyu.edu
 /event/12720048)
