SUMMARY:Hangeul Day
DESCRIPTION:EAS Presents Hangeul DayDepartment of East Asian Studies (EAS
 )\, in collaboration with KISO\, proudly presents Hangeul Day. Hangeul Da
 y is a national holiday in South Korea\, celebrated on October 9th each y
 ear. It commemorates the creation and proclamation of the Korean writing 
 system\, Hangeul\, by King Sejong the Great in 1443. The day is marked by
  various cultural events\, exhibitions\, and educational programs that hi
 ghlight the significance of Hangeul in Korean history and culture. The ev
 ent will feature interactive Korean language workshop stations where part
 icipants can learn and practice the basics of Hangeul. Additionally\, att
 endees can enjoy calligraphy\, traditional crafts\, games\, and experienc
 e the elegance of hanbok\, the traditional Korean attire. This celebratio
 n will be a vibrant showcase of Korean heritage and language. Come and jo
 in us! This event is presented by the Department of East Asian Studies an
 d co-sponsored by KISO.Hosted by: Department of East Asian StudiesAdditio
 nal Information can be found at: https://engage.nyu.edu/event/12481163 (h
 ttps://engage.nyu.edu/event/12481163)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:EAS Presents Hangeul DayDepartment of East A
 sian Studies (EAS)\, in collaboration with KISO\, proudly presents Hangeu
 l Day. Hangeul Day is a national holiday in South Korea\, celebrated on O
 ctober 9th each year. It commemorates the creation and proclamation of th
 e Korean writing system\, Hangeul\, by King Sejong the Great in 1443. The
  day is marked by various cultural events\, exhibitions\, and educational
  programs that highlight the significance of Hangeul in Korean history an
 d culture. The event will feature interactive Korean language workshop st
 ations where participants can learn and practice the basics of Hangeul. A
 dditionally\, attendees can enjoy calligraphy\, traditional crafts\, game
 s\, and experience the elegance of hanbok\, the traditional Korean attire
