DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T133000
SUMMARY:Supporting Neurodivergent Learners: Practical Strategies for Home
  and School\, featuring Dr. Conner Black\, Child Mind Institute
DESCRIPTION:Raising a neurodivergent child brings distinct joys and uniqu
 e challenges\, but finding reliable\, evidence-based guidance doesn't hav
 e to be a struggle. NYU Work Life is partnering with the Child Mind Insti
 tute (https://childmind.org/) to give parents grounded\, actionable tools
  to help school-aged children flourish academically and emotionally. Gain
  expert guidance on boosting your child's self-advocacy while building st
 rong\, collaborative partnerships with their educators.  Session Highligh
 ts:  - Empowering Your Child: Actionable ways to build confidence\, self-
 awareness\, and self-advocacy skills in school-aged learners.  - School P
 artnerships: Effective strategies for collaborating with teachers and sch
 ool support teams.  - Navigating Accommodations: Practical guidance on ad
 vocating for the right classroom supports and services your child needs t
 o succeed.About the Speaker:Dr. Conner Black (https://childmind.org/bio/c
 onner-james-black-phd/) is a clinical psychologist and Associate Director
  of the Autism Center at the Child Mind Institute\, who supervises a mult
 idisciplinary clinical team and supports the integration of research into
  clinical practice to address the most pressing needs of patients and fam
 ilies. Specializing in diagnostic assessment and care for children and yo
 ung adults with ASD and related conditions\, Dr. Black works extensively 
 with families\, schools\, and organizations to foster inclusive\, support
 ive environments for neurodivergent individuals.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Raising a neurodivergent child brings d
 istinct joys and unique challenges\, but finding reliable\, evidence-base
 d guidance doesn't have to be a struggle. NYU Work Life is partnering wit
 h the <a href="https://childmind.org/">Child Mind Institute</a> to give p
 arents grounded\, actionable tools to help school-aged children flourish 
 academically and emotionally. Gain expert guidance on boosting your child
 's self-advocacy while building strong\, collaborative partnerships with 
 their educators.</p><p>  Session Highlights:<br />  - Empowering Your Chi
 ld: Actionable ways to build confidence\, self-awareness\, and self-advoc
 acy skills in school-aged learners.<br />  - School Partnerships: Effecti
 ve strategies for collaborating with teachers and school support teams.<b
 r />  - Navigating Accommodations: Practical guidance on advocating for t
 he right classroom supports and services your child needs to succeed.</p>
 <p><strong>About the Speaker:</strong><a href="https://childmind.org/bio/
 conner-james-black-phd/">Dr. Conner Black</a> is a clinical psychologist 
 and Associate Director of the Autism Center at the Child Mind Institute\,
  who supervises a multidisciplinary clinical team and supports the integr
 ation of research into clinical practice to address the most pressing nee
 ds of patients and families. Specializing in diagnostic assessment and ca
 re for children and young adults with ASD and related conditions\, Dr. Bl
 ack works extensively with families\, schools\, and organizations to fost
 er inclusive\, supportive environments for neurodivergent individuals.</p
 >
