LOCATION:NYU Kimmel Center\, Room 803<br />\n60 Washington Square S\, New
  York\, NY 10012
SUMMARY:NYU Alumni and Families Weekend: Generally Recognized as "Safe"? 
 Debunking the Myths of U.S. Food Regulation
DESCRIPTION:Join us for NYU's Alumni &amp\; Families Weekend 2026 to reco
 nnect with fellow GPH alumni!&#160\;For decades\, a regulatory loophole h
 as allowed the food industry to introduce hundreds of new chemical substa
 nces directly into our food supply without ever notifying the public or t
 he FDA. How did we get here\, and what does it mean for the future of pub
 lic health? NYU School of Global Public Health Professor Jennifer Pomeran
 z will take you behind the headlines to reveal how the "Generally Recogni
 zed As Safe" loophole works\, why it primarily impacts ultra-processed fo
 ods\, and the policy reforms required to fix a broken system.https://publ
 ichealth.nyu.edu/events-news/events/2026/10/24/nyu-alumni-and-families-we
 ekend-generally-recognized-safe-debunking (https://publichealth.nyu.edu/e
 vents-news/events/2026/10/24/nyu-alumni-and-families-weekend-generally-re
 cognized-safe-debunking)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join us for NYU's Alumni &amp\; Families Wee
 kend 2026 to reconnect with fellow GPH alumni!&#160\;For decades\, a regu
 latory loophole has allowed the food industry to introduce hundreds of ne
 w chemical substances directly into our food supply without ever notifyin
 g the public or the FDA. How did we get here\, and what does it mean for 
 the future of public health? NYU School of Global Public Health Professor
  Jennifer Pomeranz will take you behind the headlines to reveal how the "
 Generally Recognized As Safe" loophole works\, why it primarily impacts u
 ltra-processed foods\, and the policy reforms required to fix a broken sy
 stem.<br /><a href="https://publichealth.nyu.edu/events-news/events/2026/
 10/24/nyu-alumni-and-families-weekend-generally-recognized-safe-debunking
 " target="_blank">https://publichealth.nyu.edu/events-news/events/2026/10
 /24/nyu-alumni-and-families-weekend-generally-recognized-safe-debunking</
 a>
