DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261025T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261025T160000
LOCATION:Battery Maritime Building\, 10 South Street\, New York\, NY 10004
GEO:40.7009;-74.01183
SUMMARY:Discover NY: Fall for Governors Island!
DESCRIPTION:This event is intended for NYU international students/scholar
 s and the NYU community.  Trade the subway for a ferry. Just 7 minutes fr
 om Lower Manhattan\, Governors Island has 172 car-free acres and the best
  Statue of Liberty views in the city\, and we're heading there on its mos
 t festive weekend of the fall.  For one weekend only\, Nolan Park\, just 
 a 3-minute walk from the ferry\, becomes a free pumpkin patch and fall fe
 stival (event page (https://www.govisland.com/things-to-do/events/pumpkin
 -point-2026)). Pick your own pumpkin and paint it\, go trick-or-treating 
 at the historic houses\, and catch a ghost tour\, a fall foliage walk or 
 some live folk music.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>This event is intended for NYU in
 ternational students/scholars and the NYU community.</strong></p><p>  Tra
 de the subway for a ferry. Just 7 minutes from Lower Manhattan\, Governor
 s Island has 172 car-free acres and the best Statue of Liberty views in t
 he city\, and we're heading there on its most festive weekend of the fall
 .</p><p>  For one weekend only\, Nolan Park\, just a 3-minute walk from t
 he ferry\, becomes a free pumpkin patch and fall festival (<a href="https
 ://www.govisland.com/things-to-do/events/pumpkin-point-2026">event page</
 a>). Pick your own pumpkin and paint it\, go trick-or-treating at the his
 toric houses\, and catch a ghost tour\, a fall foliage walk or some live 
 folk music.</p>
UID:20261025T140000Z-407308@events.nyu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261002T163810Z
URL:https://events.nyu.edu/event/407308-discover-ny-fall-for-governors-is
 land
CATEGORIES:Free,Students
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T180348Z
